cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "analog-ready: Analog Robustness CI for AI accelerators"
authors:
  - family-names: Demirel
    given-names: Omer
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-01
repository-code: "https://github.com/demirelo/analog-ready"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A PyTorch toolchain that answers whether an AI model survives analog in-memory
  compute (PCM/ReRAM/SRAM crossbars) or photonic hardware: a per-op break-even
  envelope (converter energy, weight reuse, ENOB precision), a simulation ladder
  (programming noise, conductance drift, ADC quantization, end-of-life composition),
  and a redaction-safe reporting/regression-gate surface. All simulation
  coefficients are literature defaults, not measured silicon; limits are disclosed
  at the point of use.
